<title>SWITZERLAND: BOBSLEIGH-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BOBSLEIGH-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ST. MORITZ, Switzerland 1997-01-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings</p>
<p>after two-of-four runs at the bobsleigh world championship</p>
<p>two-man</p>
<p>competition on Saturday (third and fourth runs on Sunday):</p>
<p>1.Switzerland I (Reto Goetschi/Guido Acklin) two minutes, 9.10</p>
<p>seconds (first run 1:04.55/second run 1:04.55)</p>
<p>2. Italy I (Guenther Huber/Antonio Tartaglia) 2:09.43 (1:04.54/</p>
<p>1:04.89)</p>
<p>3. U.S. I (Brian Shimer/Robert Olesen) 2:09.49</p>
<p>(1:04.74/1:04.75)</p>
<p>4. Germany I (Sepp Dostthaler/Thomas Platzer) 2:09.53 (1:04.58/</p>
<p>1:04.95)</p>
<p>5. Canada I (Pierre Lueders/Dave MacEachern) 2:09.54 (1:04.73/</p>
<p>1:04.91)  6. Canada II (Chris Lori/Sheridan Baptiste) 2:09.68</p>
<p>(1:04.71/ 1:04.97)</p>
<p>7. Latvia I (Sandis Prusis/Adris Pluksna) 2:10.02 (1:04.87/</p>
<p>1:05.15)</p>
<p>8. Germany II (Matthias Benesch/Lars Bolte) 2:10.21 (1:05.03/</p>
<p>1:05.18)</p>
<p>9. U.S. II (Jim Herberich/Garrettt Hines) 2:10.29 (1:05.10/</p>
<p>1:05.06)</p>
<p>10. Britain I (Sean Olsson/Dean Ward) 2:10.36 (1:05.101:05.26)</p>
